# Calculation unit tests

All logic in `src/calculations/` must have coverage in `tests/`.

## Test file mapping

| Source | Tests |
|--------|-------|
| `mortgageCalculator.js` | `tests/mortgageCalculator.test.js` |
| `amortizationSchedule.js` | `tests/amortizationSchedule.test.js` |
| `paymentScenarios.js` | `tests/paymentScenarios.test.js` |
| `timeToPayoff.js` | `tests/timeToPayoff.test.js` |
| `investmentComparison.js` | `tests/investmentComparison.test.js` |
| `formatters.js` | `tests/formatters.test.js` |

## Baseline scenarios to preserve

Default app inputs (2M SEK loan, 3M property, 500k income, 3.5% rate, 30 years):

- Monthly amortization ≈ 1,667 SEK
- Monthly interest ≈ 5,833 SEK
- Total monthly payment = 7,500 SEK
- Amortization rate = 1%

## Adding or changing calculations

1. Write or update tests first when fixing bugs; update tests after when changing requirements.
2. Use `toBeCloseTo` for floating-point money values.
3. Assert structure (array lengths, required fields) in addition to numeric outputs.
4. Run `npm test` before every push.
